aiproof (0.1.12) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First-attempt formatting: the prompt now states the input's exact line
    count per request ("THIS INPUT HAS EXACTLY 4 LINES...") — small models
    obey a concrete number far better than abstract newline rules. Dropped
    line breaks were the dominant guard rejection (journal: 4->3, 5->4,
    3->1 collapses), each one costing a retry LLM call. With qwen2.5:3b
    every eval case now passes formatting on the first attempt; score up
    from 14/20 to 17/21. New multiline-collapse eval case.

 -- Ed Watson <edmundwatson@gmail.com>  Wed, 16 Sep 2026 14:00:00 +0200

aiproof (0.1.11) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Ollama requests now send keep_alive (config ollama_keep_alive, default
    30m): Ollama's own 5-minute eviction meant a 9-40s cold model reload on
    the next proofread — the single largest real-world latency source.

 -- Ed Watson <edmundwatson@gmail.com>  Wed, 16 Sep 2026 09:30:00 +0200

aiproof (0.1.10) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Context-aware proofreading (opt-in, requires saved history): a consensus
    profile is mined from history — domain vocabulary the model must not
    "correct" (words that survived >=2 proofreads, dictionary-filtered with
    case-aware rules and typo edit-distance checks) plus a one-sentence LLM
    domain summary regenerated in the background every ~25 proofreads.
    Injected as a small capped block into the prompt: zero LLM calls on the
    hot path, ~100 extra prompt tokens. Inspect with 'aiproof context'
    (--refresh, --clear); 'history --clear' also clears the learned context.
    Settings toggle on the Behavior page. Evals pin the flag off for
    determinism (opt in with --context). Recommends wamerican (word list;
    shape-based fallback without it).

 -- Ed Watson <edmundwatson@gmail.com>  Tue, 15 Sep 2026 10:00:00 +0200

aiproof (0.1.9) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Opt-in proofread history: every completed proofread (original,
    corrected, source flow, provider/model, pipeline path, timing) is
    appended to ~/.local/share/aiproof/history.jsonl (created 0600).
    Off by default — it stores your text. Toggle in settings (Behavior
    page); view with 'aiproof history [--tail N | --clear | --path]'.

 -- Ed Watson <edmundwatson@gmail.com>  Thu, 20 Aug 2026 10:25:00 +0200

aiproof (0.1.8) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Flow hardening: clipboard snapshot failures now notify instead of
    crashing the run; whitespace-only selections are rejected before the
    model (both flows); a network failure during the format-repair call
    now triggers provider failover instead of reporting "Couldn't apply
    corrections safely"; connect timeouts report the host as unreachable;
    the "ydotool not set up" note no longer appears when clipboard-only
    mode was chosen deliberately; "No changes needed" says when the
    fallback provider served the check.
  * Every flow branch now logs its decision (orchestrator gates, retries,
    guard rejections, salvage skips, fallback failures, CLI outcomes).
  * 81 fully mocked flow tests covering every route (orchestrator, LLM
    pipeline, provider failover, CLI, DBus dispatch); make test-flow
    writes a route-by-route log report to build/flow-report.md.
  * docs/flow.md: mermaid flow charts (simple + detailed) of every route.

  * "No changes needed" notifications now quote the text that was checked
    (up to 60 chars), so a capture mismatch — wrong selection, stale
    clipboard — is immediately visible instead of reading as a missed typo.
  * Captured selection content is logged at DEBUG level (aiproof -v daemon)
    for diagnosing capture issues; the default journal still gets only
    counts, never content.
  * Eval: single-word typo + single-word clean canary cases.

 -- Ed Watson <edmundwatson@gmail.com>  Fri, 14 Aug 2026 10:30:00 +0200

aiproof (0.1.7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fallback provider: optional second provider/endpoint/model tried
    automatically when the primary is unreachable or fails (e.g. local
    Ollama for when the remote GPU box is away). Configurable in the
    settings window; notifications and CLI say when the fallback was used.
  * 5s connect timeout so an unreachable host fails over in seconds
    instead of hanging for the full request timeout.

 -- Ed Watson <edmundwatson@gmail.com>  Mon, 11 Aug 2026 15:25:00 +0200

aiproof (0.1.6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Honest reporting: when every correction is rejected by the safety
    guards, say "Couldn't apply corrections safely" instead of the
    misleading "No changes needed" (notification + CLI warning).
  * Segment salvage for single-line text: when whole-text correction keeps
    getting rejected, split on sentence/clause boundaries and correct each
    segment independently (separators, fragment case, and end punctuation
    preserved) — partial fixes now get through on messy chat-style text.
  * New guards: added angle brackets (models wrapping URLs in <...>) and
    added question/exclamation marks (statements turned into questions).

 -- Ed Watson <edmundwatson@gmail.com>  Thu, 24 Jul 2026 10:15:00 +0200

